From: boingbasti <boingbasti@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:33:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 32/49] avformat/dashdec: explicit http options for byte range
 segments

Byte range segments (several segments share one file) get seekable=1
and reconnect=1 instead of the auto default, which is more robust when
the connection breaks in the middle of a range request.

Ported to FFmpeg 9.0.2 from ffmpeg-dash-http-options.patch.
Port: the patch was written for a tree without skyjet18's seg->seekable.
The standalone segment part (seekable=0 + multiple_requests=1) is already
done by skyjet18's 'set optimal http settings based on media type', so
only the byte range case (seg->size >= 0) is added to the seekable
branch. Subtitles keep skyjet18's seekable=0.
---
 libavformat/dashdec.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/dashdec.c b/libavformat/dashdec.c
index efbc300b..8e0e7b17 100644
--- a/libavformat/dashdec.c
+++ b/libavformat/dashdec.c
@@ -1964,9 +1964,11 @@ static int open_input(DASHContext *c, struct representation *pls, struct fragmen
         /* disable seeking for subtitles - subtitles are small and many servers doesn't support byterange for subtitles */
         av_dict_set(&opts, "seekable", "0", 0);
     }
-    else if(seg->seekable)
+    else if(seg->seekable || seg->size >= 0)
     {
-        /* single big segment - allow seeking and reconnect if needed */
+        /* single big segment or byte range segment (several segments share
+         * one file) - allow seeking and reconnect if needed, more robust when
+         * the connection breaks in the middle of a range request */
         av_dict_set(&opts, "seekable", "1", 0);
         av_dict_set(&opts, "reconnect", "1", 0);
     }
